class:: HenonSonify
summary:: Explicit Hénon-map clock and level sonifier
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/HenonMap, Classes/GbmanSonify

description::

Uses the same recurrence as link::Classes/HenonMap::, but explicitly folds one selected coordinate into an iteration-frequency range and another into -1 through 1. Frequency is limited to the audio sample rate and at most one iteration occurs per sample.

Interpolation 0 holds, 1 is linear, and 2 uses a zero-slope cubic Hermite segment. Unlike link::Classes/HenonMap::, this class is an audio sonifier rather than a raw mathematical-state generator.

subsection:: Visualizing the internal dynamics

See link::Classes/HenonMap:: for the recurrence's static portrait and exact-state live view. The sonifier does not expose its internal coordinates, so running a second map beside it would not be a synchronized visualization of the sound.

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: minFreq
Mapped minimum iteration frequency in hertz.
argument:: maxFreq
Mapped maximum iteration frequency in hertz.
argument:: clockLo
Lower folding bound for the clock coordinate.
argument:: clockHi
Upper folding bound for the clock coordinate.
argument:: outputLo
Lower folding bound for the level coordinate.
argument:: outputHi
Upper folding bound for the level coordinate.
argument:: clockIndex
Init-rate coordinate: 0 x, 1 y.
argument:: outputIndex
Init-rate coordinate: 0 x, 1 y.
argument:: interp
Init-rate code: 0 hold, 1 linear, 2 cubic Hermite.
argument:: a
Hénon quadratic coefficient.
argument:: b
Hénon old-x coupling coefficient.
argument:: x0
Initial x state.
argument:: y0
Initial y state.
argument:: reset
Restore map, phase, and interpolation state.
argument:: mul
Output multiplier.
argument:: add
Output offset.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ HenonSonify.ar * 0.08 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ HenonSonify.ar(40, 8000, interp: 1) * 0.08 }.play
)
::

